Russian text (runs tagged `ru`) had no proofing at all: no spelling marks, no grammar, and English hyphenation patterns applied to Cyrillic. This adds Russian alongside English and Polish, following the Polish design (`crates/proof/src/ru/`, same affix engine, same `ProofLang` plumbing).

**Spelling.** Against a Russian Hunspell dictionary installed on the system, never bundled: `ru_RU` from the OS, a package manager, LibreOffice's `dict-ru` (now searched on Windows, macOS and Linux) or `WORDCRAFT_DICTIONARIES`. The loader also decodes KOI8-R and Windows-1251, which older Russian dictionaries use. Russian-specific acceptance:
- `ё` is optional, as in ordinary writing (`елка`/`ёлка`, `еще`/`ещё`), whichever form the dictionary lists;
- hyphenated words are checked whole, then by parts, knowing particles (`кто-то`, `где-нибудь`, `всё-таки`), `кое-`, `по-` adverbs (`по-русски` via `русский`, `по-новому`), linking vowels (`северо-западный`) and abbreviation parts (`ИИ-консультант`);
- solid compounds (`высокоэластичный`, `газоиспользующий`), `не` with adjectives, participles and verbal nouns (`невскрытый`, `неисполнение`; never verbs, so `незнаю` stays wrong), productive prefixes (`ультра-`, `эко-`, `микро-`) and prefixed verbs;
- abbreviations with endings (`ГИПа`, `ПДн`), camel case (`ВКонтакте`) and words with superscripts (`м²`) are left alone;
- `assets/spelling/ru-extra.txt`: our own supplement (~200 base forms with declension classes, expanded in `ru/extra.rs`) for words older dictionaries lack: `маркетплейс`, `промокод`, `интеграция`, `бонусный`, `колеровать`… Attributed in `ATTRIBUTION.md`.

**Suggestions.** Russian dictionaries carry no `MAP`/`REP`, so the letter groups and confusions are defined in code: `е`/`ё` first, unstressed vowels, voiced/voiceless pairs, `ь`/`ъ`, `жы`/`чя`, `тся`/`ться`, doubled and unpronounced consonants (`здраствуй` → `здравствуй`), missing spaces (`незнаю` → `не знаю`, but no "preposition + verb" splits), one typo, then a stem scan…

## #1093: clicks on ribbon and status-bar chrome keep typing in the document

Fixes #1093. egui takes focus away from a widget whenever the user clicks somewhere else. Ribbon command buttons gave it back to the page (#686), but galleries, tab names, check boxes, empty ribbon space and status-bar items didn't. Now `WordApp::refocus_after_chrome_click` gives focus back to the page after any click on window chrome that leaves nothing focused, so the caret stays and typing continues, as in Word.

Focus is left alone for:
- text fields (font size, zoom, command search);
- dialogs, menus and popups;
- Backstage and selected comment balloons.

Tabs, style tiles and status-bar items now report their names to screen readers. The view buttons' tooltips read "Web Layout", "Print Layout" and "Read Mode" instead of raw ids.

**Tests:** regression test `clicks_on_ribbon_and_status_bar_chrome_keep_typing_in_the_document` covers:
- a gallery tile, tab names and a View check box;
- empty ribbon space;
- the status-bar view buttons;
- the language menu, opened then cancelled;
- the font size box keeping its focus.

`cargo xtask ci` passes.

